rty. I'm the oldest in the research institute besides the director.\" [378] \"Wow, you retire at forty? What happens then?\" Sugawara was puzzled. [379] \"We get a pension, which is quite substantial. It lasts for a while. After that, if we want, we can go back to work. With our experience, there are plenty of job opportunities.\" [380] \"That's impressive,\" Sugawara nodded vigorously. \"That shows high levels of ability. If only universities were like that...\"\n[381] The slow boat they were on finally reached the other side of the estuary and left the dam. The waves on the sea became slightly larger, but the weather was sunny, there was no wind, and the sea was still calm. Several small fishing boats floated on the sea, and young people riding on single-person motorboats could still be seen in the distance. The boat was heading south towards the high-hanging sun. [382] M\u00e9ngr\u00ecn walked towards Shuzhuang and Shengen from the cockpit. [383] \"Can I ask you about Dr. Shinobu Akagi?\" M\u00e9ngr\u00ecn asked Shengen, \"About Dr. Akagi killing her parents...\"\n[384] \"West Garden, don't be so impolite.\" Shuzhuang said. [385] \"No, it's okay. It's not something that needs to be particularly concealed.\" Shengen smiled bitterly, \"Don't take it to heart... We don't have much common sense about etiquette... You can see my appearance.\" [386] Indeed. The deputy director came out to greet the guests without tying his tie and shaving his beard. Sugawa thought that the employees of the research institute on the isolated island were a group of superhumans. [387] \"Do you know about the incident fifteen years ago?\" Mio asked. [388] \"No, I don't. I went there after that,\" Yamanaka answered. \"So I haven't met Dr. Shinobu Momiji Left-san, and I haven't met Dr. Shinobu Momiji Mei-chan either.\" [389] \"What happened?\" Mio's delicate wrist rested on the back of the bench. [390] \"What happened?\" Yamanaka looked puzzled. [391] \"She loves to hear such things. It's not a good hobby,\" Shin'en said, lighting a cigarette. \"She just reads murder novels.\" [392] \"They are mystery novels,\" Mizuho corrected. [393] \"As far as I know... the incident happened at the research institute, right?\" Shin'en asked Shin'en. [394] \"Yes, it was when the research institute was being built halfway. The island wasn't a private property yet. At that time, Ms. Akira Mizuhara was fourteen years old. However, as a child prodigy, she was famous not only in the field of computers but also throughout the country. I went to work at the research institute because I admired her. She killed her parents, Dr. Akira Mizuhara and Dr. Mei Chien Mizuhara, with a knife in her own room.\" Shin'en spoke without emotion. [395] \"Were there any witnesses at the time?\" Mizuho asked immediately. [396] \"Yeah, she was caught by Ms. Akita's uncle... the current director... at the crime scene. The director's wife also saw it. I heard it directly from the director.\" [397] \"A 14-year-old girl killed two people without any interference?\" Maki asked. [398] \"I don't know,\" Mountain shook his head. [399] \"She told me... her doll killed her parents. What does that mean?\" Maki recalled what Ms. Akita said. [400] \"Ah, I know that too. Ms. Akita has multiple personalities.\" Mountain answered casually. [401] \"I've heard a little about it.\" Kurosu agreed. [402] \"I always feel like I don't quite understand... but the treating doctor said so, and the court acquitted her. You can understand it by talking to her. I thought it was a joke at first.\" [403] \"How did you know?\" Momo straightened up. [404] \"When I met Ms. Nishiyama, she said she was Ms. Matsutani Shiki...\" Yamane wiped the sweat off his forehead, \"uh...yeah.\" [405] \"Hmm, yes, she said that herself.\" Momo answered. [406] \"Sayuri Higashida sometimes speaks like a man,\" Yamamoto explained. \"When you ask her again, she'll say her name is Kazuo. Everyone at the lab knows. I watched the video too. She said the killer was a doll... not another personality, right?\" [407] \"Why did she say 'doll'?\" asked Mouri. \"Do you mean a personality like a doll?\" [408] \"No, just a figment of my imagination,\" Yamamoto smiled. \"Anyway, any personality she has is top-notch in terms of work. She's a genius in programming. Her talents remain intact. It was Sayuri Higashida, Ph.D., who made the Higashida Research Institute what it is today. Our work relies entirely on her guidance. She'll tell you anything if you ask her.\" [409] \"So, where is Sayuri Higashida Ph.D. in the lab? Is she really on the island?\" Mouri asked an odd question. [410] \"Ha, yes, that's understandable,\" Yamamoto laughed in response. \"Indeed, you can only see her on TV. But she's actually in a certain place underground in the lab. Her living quarters are on the west side of the second floor underground, taking up about a quarter of that floor. That's around six rooms... maybe it's more accurate to say she's been isolated since that incident. There's only one door, always under strict surveillance. Sayuri Higashida hasn't left that place in fifteen years. Well, the lab itself is a bit strange too... no windows at all. We work almost like her in a sealed environment.\" [411] \"Secret room\" was a new term for Kamata. [412] \"Who can enter Dr. Akagi's place?\" Mizuki asked. [413] \"No one can,\" Nagano said. \"After the murder incident, no one from the outside could, and no one in the lab could meet her directly. Moreover, Dr. Akagi herself refuses to meet anyone. As far as I know... she's completely cut off from the outside world. The network is monitored, and sending personal emails doesn't work. Sending her things personally is also not allowed.\" [414] \"That's to prevent any leaks of secrets, I guess,\" Kamata said, taking a drag of his cigarette. [415] \"There's that aspect to it, too,\" Nagano answered. \"Meeting with Dr. Akagi cannot be done in a private setting. We need several people to monitor and 