ed sign for tourism, but it was no longer legible. Next to the sign, there was a four-wheel drive car parked on a grassy, overgrown patch of land. [426] \"It's about a fifteen-minute walk from here to the campsite. Please put the heavy luggage on top of the car. I can only carry four people besides me. S\u014dma-sensei and\u2026 ah, two ladies\u2026 let's prioritize the ladies and send them first.\" The two ladies referred to were Nishimura Momiji and the exchange student Xiao Wu. [427] \"And one more person,\" S\u014dma pointed to Kuni, \"I forgot to introduce her. She is my assistant Kuni-san. She is the most skilled in designing programs among us, and I am second\u2026\"\n[428] A tall woman with a straw hat, Kuni-sono, approached. She was not wearing makeup, and her head was shaved very short. Her tall stature made it difficult to recognize her as a woman. [429] \"I'll walk there,\" Kuni said reluctantly. However, she was always reluctant, and it may not be because she was in a bad mood.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 2:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:35 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \n[1177] \"Hmm, the last one to open the door was Mr. Yamanaka,\" Ito-san said in a trembling voice, \"Two o'clock fourteen minutes... just now.\" [1178] \"What about before?\" Yamanaka asked. [1179] \"It was also Mr. Yamanaka... One o'clock forty-three minutes...\" Ito-san's voice sounded like she was about to cry. [1180] \"Not that door...\u201d Yamanaka said immediately, \"It's another exit.\" [1181] Ito-san moved that window to the back and clicked the mouse again. A new window appeared in its original position, and a list suddenly appeared. [1182] \"It was Waga-san,\" Ito-san read the list, \"at 1:44... before that, it was this morning yesterday...\"\n[1183] Mr. Yamane whistled. \"Strange... impossible... absolutely impossible.\" [1184] \"Deborah is not completely reliable,\"