ase tell him to come over.\" New Vine's wife said. [1001] Mina realized what she meant by \"that person\" only after a while. She took the hand of the confused Miss Akagi, who was looking around, and got on the elevator, closing the door. Mina saw the display light on the door stop at 1. [1002] \"Now we just have to wait for the police,\" said Nagao, letting out a sigh of relief. \"Miss Nishizumi, do you know any police officers?\" [1003] \"Yes, my uncle is in the county police department,\" Mina answered cautiously. Mina's uncle, the younger brother of her deceased father, was the head of the Aichi Prefectural Police Department. He is now Mina's closest relative and guardian. \"How long will it take the police to arrive?\" [1004] \"It would take a while if they come by helicopter... But they'll probably come by boat. It's about an hour,\" said Nagao, puffing on a cigarette. [1005] Mina looked around the room. Ms. Tomita was tapping her shoulder at the computer. Professor Kusaka was staring blankly at the screen behind her. Mr. Suzuki, who was sitting at another computer earlier, was nowhere to be seen. Dr. Nakayama and his wife were sitting in a chair in the corner of the room, looking tired. Through the glass, Mina could see Koyama-san in the next room. The body wrapped in a sheet still stood in the corridor. Mina thought it was good that Miss Akagi didn't have to walk through the corridor. [1006] Miyuki looked around the room. Ms. Shimada was tapping her shoulder at the computer. Professor Kumagai was staring blankly at the screen behind her. Mr. Mizuguchi, who was sitting at another computer earlier, was nowhere to be seen. The Doctor and his wife were sitting in a chair in the corner of the room, looking tired. Dr. Kawaguchi could be seen through the glass in the adjacent room. The body covered with a sheet still stood in the hallway. Miyuki thought that it was fortunate that Miss Akutagawa didn't have to walk through the hallway. [1007] Miyuki walked over to Professor Kumagai and sat down in the chair next to him. [1008] \"That person was Dr. Akutagawa's younger sister, wasn't she?\" Professor Kumagai whispered to Miyuki. \"Does she only speak English?\" [1009] \"Yes, it seems so,\" Miyuki nodded. \"She came back to Japan to see her sister...\"\n[1010] \"Have you contacted the police?\" Professor Kumagai asked. [1011] \"How did Hoshino get down the elevator?\" Kumigawa asked, fumbling for a cigarette, \"Are there any other ways to get to the roof?\" [1012] \"Yes, he was already on the roof.\" The girl replied. [1013] \"Hey, West Garden\u2026\" Kumigawa exhaled smoke, his expression serious, \"I've been thinking. Dr. True Aridaka's body appeared there, and then when we went to the hallway\u2026did everyone leave the room?\" [1014] \"Miss. Tateyama is here.\" The girl leaned forward and said, \"Professor, what did you think of?\" [1015] \"Miss Tateyama fainted here.\" Kumigawa lowered his voice so that the nearby Miss Tateyama wouldn't hear, \"Everyone went to the hallway to see the bride. Was the yellow door open then?\" [1016] \"Yes, it was,\" nodded Momiji. [1017] \"So the killer could have come out from there and taken the elevator. Right... I saw the elevator door open with barely any sound. It was noisy then, and we all rushed to the hallway to see Dr. Makoto's body. Even if someone got on the elevator...,\" Nishikawa said, \"But it's impossible. I saw the recording from the opposite room. The entire room's situation was recorded. Want to see it?\" [1018] \"Okay...,\" Nishikawa exhaled a puff of smoke, \"Then let's discard that hypothesis.\" [1019] \"More importantly, where did the killer enter?\" asked Momiji. [1020] \"What's more important is where the killer entered,\" said Momiji. [1021] \"Just analyze the VTR and we'll know,\" Naito said, \"If there's only that door as an entrance. I still don't believe it's possible.\" [1022] \"I really want to go to Ms. Makino's room and take a look,\" Momo said, her tone like